-- optimization.lth: Levenberg-Marquardt as types with laws over the array leaves: the objective
-- as a record of functions, the damping and the state of a run, one step as a theory whose
-- model is the host's or the native one, and the native driver.
--
-- Draft 0, 2026-10-14, by Claude Fable 5.1, an agent of the coordinating session, on the brief
-- record/IA/slice-theories-2-2026-10-14/prompt.md (item 3; inventory §6 item 7; the record of
-- functions crossing of D-2026-10-14-a). Sources: spec 7.R2 (over `VecOf n`), 3.S23 as it
-- stands (a record whose fields are functions crosses as the record, each a callback), 10.S10
-- (an extern validated against its type's laws), 11.S18 (a tolerance is the demand's), 7.R4
-- (per model), 4.R10, P11 (every criterion is a parameter: the damping schedule, v0.1's
-- `muInit`, `muFactor`, `muMin`, `muMax`, and the settings of belief.lth). The v0.1 file is
-- `optimization.lut` at the tag v0.1-final; the names are its. The settings (tolerance, budget,
-- floor) and the decrement are belief.lth's, so that one `Settings` serves the maximizer and
-- the step; `pinvSym` and `trace` are arrays.lth's (added for this file, one commit each).
-- 2026-10-15, by Claude Opus 5.5, an agent of the coordinating session, on record/IA/
-- layer-3-review-2026-10-15/prompt-fix-BCD.md (items 1 and 4 of its summary-BCD.md): the gradient
-- of an objective along a drawn direction; `StepRule` determines the step from the direction: the
-- trial point and its value, accepted exactly when the value falls.
-- 2026-10-26, by Claude Opus 5.5 (night Agent V), on D-2026-10-16-m: `StopReason` moved to
-- belief.lth and `finished` gives `Maybe StopReason`; `minimizeBy` drives a model's step; §4, the
-- steps on the quadratic family derived from the definitions, the bound a Levenberg-Marquardt
-- maximizer declares, and the law that a run takes that many.
--
-- What this file states. An objective is what is minimized: a value on the vectors of a
-- dimension, its gradient and a positive step matrix (the information, or Gauss-Newton); its
-- laws tie the gradient to the value and ask the step matrix symmetric and not negative. The
-- algorithm is split into pieces that each carry a law: the damped direction, (M + mu diag M)^+
-- applied to -g at the settings' floor; one step, a trial that either accepts (the value falls,
-- the damping divides by the factor, not below the least) or rejects (the point and the value
-- stay, the damping multiplies by the factor); `finished` says why a run stops (converged by the
-- decrement, exhausted by the budget, stalled by the damping beyond its most); the driver
-- iterates the step until it does. `LMStep` is the theory of the direction and the step, with
-- the laws above and the descent of the direction; its models are the native definitions and
-- the host's (optimization_model.lut). Correctness does not depend on the path: a run that ends
-- converged is certified by the decrement at its end, recomputed from the objective, which is
-- the law `MaximizerStationary` of belief.lth on the native runner (optimization_model.lut
-- `lmMaximizer`).
--
-- Index (all sections written in this draft):
--   §1 `Objective`, its laws, `asObjective`, `posteriorOf` (v0.1 optimization.lut:16-24, 108-110). done
--   §2 `Damping`, `LMState`, `start`, `dampedStep`, `lmStep`, `finished`, `Run`, `minimizeBy`,
--      `minimize` (v0.1 optimization.lut:27-73).                                              done
--   §3 `LMStep`, the laws of a step: descent, the damping, the decrease; the quadratic family
--      (v0.1 optimization.lut:76-92).                                                         done
--   §4 `lmQuadraticSteps`, `lmQuadraticBound`, `LMStepsOnQuadratic` (2026-10-26).             done

import "numbers.lth" Tolerance Positive within withinOf abs Doubles
import "arrays.lth" Vec Mat VecOf MatOf Dim vec mat identity approxVec approxMat exact RankFloor
import "arrays_model.lut" numpy : Arrays add sub scale dot norm matVec matMul madd mscale transpose pinvSym
import "probability.lth" StepResolution IsGradient
import "belief.lth" Settings Posterior decrement quadratic quadraticReachable StopReason converged exhausted stalled isConverged

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------- §1 The objective (D-2026-10-14-a)

-- A record whose fields are functions (what crosses to the host as the record with each field
-- a callback, D-2026-10-14-a): the value on the vectors of dimension n, its gradient and the
-- step matrix. The gradient is the gradient of the value at the demand's resolution; the step
-- matrix is symmetric and its quadratic form not negative beyond rounding. Whether it
-- approximates the Hessian is a quality of the method, not a law of the objective (v0.1
-- optimization.lut:18-24). Certified per objective (7.R4), and on the quadratic family below.
Objective (n : Nat) : { value : VecOf n -> Float64, grad : VecOf n -> Vec Float64, stepMatrix : VecOf n -> Mat Float64 }
-- spec 7.R2, 11.S18
GradIsGradient (n : Nat) (o : Objective n) (r : StepResolution) (x v : VecOf n) : Bool := IsGradient n r o.value o.grad x v
StepMatrixSymmetric (n : Nat) (o : Objective n) (tol : Tolerance) (x : VecOf n) : Bool :=
  approxMat tol (o.stepMatrix x) (transpose (o.stepMatrix x))
StepMatrixNonNegative (n : Nat) (o : Objective n) (tol : Tolerance) (x v : VecOf n) : Bool :=
  { q := dot v (matVec (o.stepMatrix x) v)
    0.0 <= q or within tol q 0.0 }
Objective (n : Nat) := GradIsGradient n & StepMatrixSymmetric n & StepMatrixNonNegative n

-- a log posterior (belief.lth) as the objective that minimizes its negative, the information
-- its step matrix (v0.1 optimization.lut:108-110); and the three functions a maximizer takes,
-- as one posterior. [core bite 12] `asObjective` was `negate`, a name of the core's `Ring`.
asObjective (n : Nat) (p : Posterior n) : Objective n :=
  { value := fn x { 0.0 - p.logp x }, grad := fn x { scale (0.0 - 1.0) (p.score x) }, stepMatrix := p.info }
posteriorOf (n : Nat) (f : VecOf n -> Float64) (g : VecOf n -> Vec Float64) (m : VecOf n -> Mat Float64) : Posterior n :=
  { logp := f, score := g, info := m }

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------- §2 The damping and the state (P11)

-- The damping schedule, the method's own, a parameter (P11; v0.1 held `muInit := 0.001`,
-- `muFactor := 3.0`, `muMin := 1e-15`, `muMax := 1e15` as constants, optimization.lut:29-32):
-- the damping a run starts at, the factor it divides by on acceptance and multiplies by on
-- rejection, the least it falls to, and the most beyond which the run has stalled.
Damping : U := { init factor least most : Float64 | 0.0 < least and least <= init and init <= most and 1.0 < factor }

-- the state of a run on the vectors of dimension n: the point, its value, the damping, the
-- iterations so far, and whether the last trial was accepted (v0.1 optimization.lut:27)
LMState (n : Nat) = { x : VecOf n, phi : Float64, mu : Float64, iter : Int, accepted : Bool }

start (n : Nat) (o : Objective n) (d : Damping) (x0 : VecOf n) : LMState n :=
  { x := x0, phi := o.value x0, mu := d.init, iter := 0, accepted := true }

-- the diagonal part of a matrix
diagOf (m : Mat Float64) : Mat Float64 := mat Float64 m.m m.n (fn i j { if i == j then m.f i i else 0.0 })

-- the damped direction: (M + mu diag M)^+ applied to -g, the pseudo-inverse at the settings'
-- floor (v0.1 optimization.lut:51 solved the matrix whole)
dampedStep (n : Nat) (s : Settings) (o : Objective n) (x : VecOf n) (mu : Float64) : Vec Float64 :=
  { m := o.stepMatrix x
    scale (0.0 - 1.0) (matVec (pinvSym s.floor (madd m (mscale mu (diagOf m)))) (o.grad x)) }

-- the damping after an acceptance: divided by the factor, not below the least
lowered (d : Damping) (mu : Float64) : Float64 := if mu / d.factor > d.least then mu / d.factor else d.least

-- one trial: the value at the damped step is taken if it falls, and the damping lowered; else
-- the point and the value stay and the damping is raised (v0.1 optimization.lut:54-59)
lmStep (n : Nat) (s : Settings) (d : Damping) (o : Objective n) (st : LMState n) : LMState n :=
  { xt := add st.x (dampedStep n s o st.x st.mu)
    pt := o.value xt
    if pt < st.phi
    then { x := xt, phi := pt, mu := lowered d st.mu, iter := st.iter + 1, accepted := true }
    else { x := st.x, phi := st.phi, mu := st.mu * d.factor, iter := st.iter + 1, accepted := false } }

-- why a run stops, `StopReason` (belief.lth since 2026-10-26; core bite 12: `Reason` is also
-- checks.lth's): converged when the decrement is below the settings' tolerance, exhausted by the
-- budget, stalled by the damping beyond its most; nothing while it is running (v0.1
-- optimization.lut:63-69, where `running` was a fourth reason)
finished (n : Nat) (s : Settings) (d : Damping) (o : Objective n) (st : LMState n) : Maybe StopReason :=
  if decrement n s o.grad o.stepMatrix st.x < s.tol then just (converged unit)
  else if st.iter >= s.maxIter then just (exhausted unit)
  else if st.mu > d.most then just (stalled unit)
  else nothing

Run (n : Nat) = { state : LMState n, reason : StopReason }

-- the driver: a step iterated until the run is finished (v0.1 optimization.lut:72-73); `minimize`
-- with the native step, `minimizeBy` with a model's (§3, `LMStepsOnQuadratic`)
minimizeBy (step : (n : Nat) -> Settings -> Damping -> Objective n -> LMState n -> LMState n) (n : Nat) (s : Settings) (d : Damping) (o : Objective n) (st : LMState n) : Run n :=
  match finished n s d o st {
    nothing -> minimizeBy step n s d o (step n s d o st) ;
    just r -> { state := st, reason := r } }
minimize (n : Nat) (s : Settings) (d : Damping) (o : Objective n) (st : LMState n) : Run n := minimizeBy lmStep n s d o st

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------- §3 The laws of a step (10.S10)

-- The direction and the step as a theory of two functions, so that the host's (lm.step,
-- optimization_model.lut) is validated against them at its first action (10.S10) and the native
-- definitions above are its other model. The laws: the direction descends (its inner product
-- with the gradient is not positive beyond rounding) and agrees with the native one within the
-- demand's tolerance; the step tries the point along the direction and is accepted exactly when
-- the objective's value there is below the state's: accepted, it takes that point and that value,
-- lowers the damping by the schedule and counts the iteration; rejected, it keeps the point and
-- the value, raises the damping by the factor and counts the iteration; and on a concave quadratic
-- the first step from the start is accepted unless the start is the minimum.
LMStep : {
  direction : (n : Nat) -> Settings -> Objective n -> VecOf n -> Float64 -> Vec Float64,
  step : (n : Nat) -> Settings -> Damping -> Objective n -> LMState n -> LMState n,
}
-- spec 11.S18
DirectionDescends (m : LMStep) (tol : Tolerance) (s : Settings) (n : Dim) (o : Objective n) (x : VecOf n) (mu : Positive) : Bool :=
  { q := dot (o.grad x) (m.direction n s o x mu)
    q <= 0.0 or within tol q 0.0 }
DirectionAgrees (m : LMStep) (tol : Tolerance) (s : Settings) (n : Dim) (o : Objective n) (x : VecOf n) (mu : Positive) : Bool :=
  approxVec tol (m.direction n s o x mu) (dampedStep n s o x mu)
-- [proposed] The acceptance is an equivalence and the new value is the objective's at the trial
-- point, so that the law determines the step from the direction (4.R10): as an implication with
-- the value only bounded, `phi := pt - 1` and "accept only on even iterations" passed it
-- (summary-BCD.md, item 4). The state is any record, its `phi` unrelated to its point; the law
-- compares with `st.phi` as given, which is what `lmStep` reads.
-- spec P11 (the damping is the schedule's)
StepRule (m : LMStep) (s : Settings) (d : Damping) (n : Dim) (o : Objective n) (st : LMState n) : Bool :=
  { s2 := m.step n s d o st
    xt := add st.x (m.direction n s o st.x st.mu)
    pt := o.value xt
    s2.accepted == (pt < st.phi) and s2.iter == st.iter + 1
    and (if s2.accepted
         then approxVec exact s2.x xt and s2.phi == pt and s2.mu == lowered d st.mu
         else approxVec exact s2.x st.x and s2.phi == st.phi and s2.mu == st.mu * d.factor) }
-- the quadratic family of belief.lth, minimized: its minimum at b, curvature c
quadraticObjective (n : Nat) (b : VecOf n) (c : Positive) : Objective n := asObjective n (quadratic n b c)
QuadraticStepAccepts (m : LMStep) (s : Settings) (d : Damping) (n : Dim) (b : VecOf n) (c : Positive) (x0 : VecOf n) : Bool :=
  { o := quadraticObjective n b c
    norm (sub x0 b) == 0.0 or (m.step n s d o (start n o d x0)).accepted }
LMStep := DirectionDescends & DirectionAgrees & StepRule & QuadraticStepAccepts
-- [proposed] Three laws of `LMStep` applied to the quadratic family's objective, so that a tester
-- draws the family's parameters (an objective is a record of functions, 7.R4). They are no laws of
-- the theory beyond the three they apply; they live here, where those are stated, so that their
-- entries and their controls' have a file that claims them (L2.8, L10.12). Moved 2026-10-16 from
-- tests/tester/fit_laws.test.lut (record/IA/code-follows-2026-10-16/prompt-claim-store.md, follow-up).
DirectionDescendsOnQuadratic (m : LMStep) (tol : Tolerance) (s : Settings) (n : Dim) (b : VecOf n) (c : Positive) (x : VecOf n) (mu : Positive) : Bool :=
  DirectionDescends m tol s n (quadraticObjective n b c) x mu
DirectionAgreesOnQuadratic (m : LMStep) (tol : Tolerance) (s : Settings) (n : Dim) (b : VecOf n) (c : Positive) (x : VecOf n) (mu : Positive) : Bool :=
  DirectionAgrees m tol s n (quadraticObjective n b c) x mu
StepRuleOnQuadratic (m : LMStep) (s : Settings) (d : Damping) (n : Dim) (b : VecOf n) (c : Positive) (st : LMState n) : Bool :=
  StepRule m s d n (quadraticObjective n b c) st

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------- §4 The steps on the quadratic (D-2026-10-16-m)

-- [proposed, 2026-10-26, Agent V] How many steps the method takes on the concave quadratic of
-- belief.lth, derived from the definitions above, never a constant (P11). There the step matrix is
-- c I, so the damped direction is -(x - b) / (1 + mu) and every trial falls: the distance to the
-- maximum is multiplied by mu / (1 + mu) at each step, the decrement by its square, and the
-- damping is lowered by the schedule. From a decrement `dec` at the start the run stops converged
-- at the first k where the product brings it below the tolerance (`finished`'s strict test):
-- with v0.1's damping about six orders of magnitude at the first step and one more at each
-- following, a handful.
lmQuadraticSteps (d : Damping) (tol : Float64) (dec : Float64) (mu : Float64) (k : Nat) : Nat :=
  if dec < tol then k
  else { r := mu / (1.0 + mu)
         lmQuadraticSteps d tol (dec * r * r) (lowered d mu) (k + 1) }
-- the bound a Levenberg-Marquardt maximizer declares (belief.lth `Maximizer`'s `quadraticSteps`):
-- the count in exact arithmetic plus one step for rounding. In floating point the distance after
-- the count's k steps may exceed the exact one by the rounding of the last points, a unit in the
-- last place of b per coordinate; on belief.lth's `quadraticReachable` that leftover is within
-- the tolerance after one more step, whose factor mu / (1 + mu) is below one.
lmQuadraticBound (d : Damping) (s : Settings) (dec : Float64) : Nat := lmQuadraticSteps d s.tol dec d.init 0 + 1
-- The bound is the theory's only if a run takes that many: a model of the step, driven on the
-- quadratic family where convergence is owed and the budget is above the bound, stops converged
-- within one step of the count, the rounding either way: never fewer (a padded bound would hide
-- the alarm of D-2026-10-16-m) nor more. Over `LMStep`, so that the host's step is driven too and a step that
-- never accepts is refuted.
LMStepsOnQuadratic (m : LMStep) (fp : Doubles Float64) (s : Settings) (d : Damping) (n : Dim) (b : VecOf n) (c : Positive) (x0 : VecOf n) : Bool :=
  { o := quadraticObjective n b c
    dec := decrement n s o.grad o.stepMatrix x0
    k := lmQuadraticSteps d s.tol dec d.init 0
    if quadraticReachable fp s n b c and k + 1 <= s.maxIter
    then { r := minimizeBy m.step n s d o (start n o d x0)
           isConverged r.reason and k <= r.state.iter + 1 and r.state.iter <= k + 1 }
    else true }
-- [core bite 12] the three laws on the quadratic family, and since 2026-10-26 the steps of §4,
-- gathered so that this file claims them (4.S14), as arrays.lth gathers `ArrayContainers`
LMStepOnQuadratic := DirectionDescendsOnQuadratic & DirectionAgreesOnQuadratic & StepRuleOnQuadratic & LMStepsOnQuadratic
